# Conventions Rules (P2) — Coding & Format Standards

## C-1 — Pre-Commit Verification Checklist

Before committing to this repository, verify:
1. `python -m pytest tests/ -q` — all tests pass
2. `ruff check src/ tests/` — no lint errors
3. `ruff format --check src/ tests/` — formatting correct
4. No absolute filesystem paths introduced in agent-facing files
5. CHANGELOG updated if user-visible changes were made

Source: CP-7.

## C-2 — Lean Message Format

Inter-layer messages (TaskDispatch, StatusReport) must use the lean format defined in `schemas/lean-dispatch.yaml` and `schemas/lean-report.yaml`. Verbose prose descriptions are prohibited in dispatch/report YAML. Use verbatim compaction (key_facts lists, cause→effect notation) instead of summarization.

Source: CO-1.

## C-3 — Verbatim Extraction

`key_facts` in predecessor artifacts and `delta` in status reports must be verbatim extractions from source. Never paraphrase file paths, error messages, metric values, or commit hashes. This prevents hallucination risk per the LLM Scaling Paradox research.

Source: CO-2.

## C-4 — Tiered Line Budget

Agent-facing skill files are subject to tiered line-count ceilings:

| Tier | Ceiling | Files |
|------|---------|-------|
| Default | < 500 | `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md` |
| Large | ≤ 1000 | `workflow-system/agent/references/*.md` (24 files) |
| XL | ≤ 1600 | `workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md` (3 files) |

Verify with:
```bash
wc -l workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md workflow-system/agent/references/*.md workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md
python -m pytest tests/test_integration.py::test_skill_md_under_500_lines tests/test_reference_size_budgets.py -v
```

Source: SF-1.

## C-5 — Required Frontmatter Keys

SKILL.md frontmatter (YAML between `---` delimiters) must include ALL of: `id`, `version`, `purpose`, `triggers`, `tier`, `token_estimate`, `last_updated`, `name`, `description`. The `description` field must describe WHEN/WHY to activate the skill (trigger conditions), not WHAT the skill does.

Source: SF-2.

## C-6 — Version Consistency

The version string must match `src/devolaflow/__init__.py` `__version__` in ALL canonical 7 locations:

1. `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md` — frontmatter `version:`, banner, body "Current version:" text
2. `workflow-system/agent/workflow-skill.yaml` — identity section
3. `pyproject.toml` — version field
4. `scripts/generate_human_docs.py` — `SOURCE_VERSION`
5. `tests/test_smoke.py` — version assertion
6. `README.md` — version example (`prints "DevolaFlow vX.Y.Z"`)
7. `packages/npm/package.json` — npm installer `version` field (v17.0.0 R6; publish workflow fail-fasts on tag/version mismatch)

Two former locations are DERIVED, not pattern-managed (v14.4.0 G-031): the `README.md` version badge is a shields.io dynamic TOML badge that reads `pyproject.toml` from the GitHub raw URL at render time, and `workflow-system/human/demo/benchmark-results/index.html` derives its displayed version at load time from `version-timeline/versions.json` (newest entry; its in-file `SAMPLE_DATA` literal is a clearly-marked `file://` fallback that MAY lag and is intentionally NOT synced by `scripts/bump_version.py`).

When bumping the version, update ALL tracked locations consistently using `scripts/bump_version.py`. After bumping, run `python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v` to verify.

Source: SF-3. Absorbs W-10 (CP-3) — v15.0.0 fold per v15-ADR-004; see v15-ADR-008 §1.

## C-7 — Valid Reference Links

Every `references/xxx.md` path mentioned in SKILL.md must correspond to an actual file under `workflow-system/agent/references/`. The canonical SF-4 reference set (24 entries as of v14.0.0) is enumerated verbatim in `tests/ghost/test_registries.py::_SF4_REFERENCE_SET` (re-exported by the `tests/test_no_ghost_features.py` aggregator shim until v15.0.0) and pinned by `test_skill_reference_links_match_sf4_set` (asserts the on-disk set ↔ pinned set parity); see that fixture for the authoritative current list. Adding a NEW reference requires (a) the file under `workflow-system/agent/references/`, (b) a corresponding entry in `_SF4_REFERENCE_SET`, (c) a SKILL.md Tier-2 navigation table row, AND (d) an entry in the `references:` list of `workflow-system/agent/manifest.yaml` — the install-manifest SSOT (per A-5) from which `scripts/sync_cursor_skill.py::MIRRORED_FILES`, `scripts/install.sh`, and `devola-init` all derive their file lists (machine-readable parity linted by `tests/test_install_manifest.py`; `scripts/scaffold_reference.py` automates places (a)+(c)+(d)).

Source: SF-4.

## C-9 — Lightweight Agent Workspace Artifacts

Files inside `.local/.agent/active/<change-id>/` and
`.local/.agent/archive/<date>-<id>/` are subject to per-artifact token
budgets:

| File | Soft budget | Hard ceiling |
|------|-------------|--------------|
| goal.md | 200 | 400 |
| checklist.md | 1200 | 2400 |
| stage.md | 400 | 800 |
| preflight.md | 600 | 1200 |
| spec.md | 1500 | 3000 |
| STATUS.yaml | 150 | 300 |
| owned_files.txt | 50 | 100 |
| Handoff envelope | 600 | 1200 |
| evidence/ | No token limit | ≤ 10 KB/file; ≤ 50 KB/directory |

The `.local/human/` surface (v14.0.0) carries its own per-artifact token
budgets (TOKENS are the sole enforced unit; line/word figures are
authoring guidance only):

| File | Soft budget | Hard ceiling |
|------|-------------|--------------|
| `.local/human/input/constitution.md` | 800 | 1500 |
| `.local/human/input/requirements.md` | 1200 | 2500 |
| `.local/human/input/requirements/<domain>.md` (shard, per-file) | 1200 | 2500 |
| `.local/human/input/amendments/<date>-<slug>.md` (per-file) | 400 | 800 |
| `.local/human/output/DIGEST.md` | 600 | 1000 |
| `.local/human/output/convergence/<version>-convergence.md` | 700 | 1000 |

Verify with:
```bash
python -m devolaflow.agent_workspace.lint <change-id>   # agent-workspace artifacts
python -c "from devolaflow.agent_workspace import lint_human; print(lint_human())"  # .local/human/ surface
```
Soft budget over → warn. Hard ceiling over → fail commit.

Source: v15-ADR-008 §C-9; human-surface details in `references/human-surface.md` §4c.
